{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>and he dwells at the haven of the sea.</b> Since it said above: מזה לחוף ימים ישכון — and there are towns that stand on a sea port, but the city is somewhat distant from the sea, and there is trouble for ship owners to go from the shore of the sea to the city by land — therefore sometimes they refrain from entering that port and travel farther to another city, even though it is farther away, because it is close to the shore of the sea near the ships. Therefore he returned and said: והוא לחוף אניות — to say that his towns will be close indeed to the place where the ships come there."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:26.610674847Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}